{"id":"2001372387644563990","kind":"article","title":"在你成功复习其前置课程之前，Execute Program 的课程不会解锁","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zHLWyC5LVXZLWE9RmoC1gua"],"publisher":"Jarrett Ye","column":"助记媒介 & 思想工具","date":"2026-02-01","updated":"2026-10-27","votes":9,"comment_count":0,"minutes":2,"chars":720,"keywords":["助记媒介","间隔重复","课程设计","前置知识","学习路径","Execute Program"],"summary":"作者解释，Execute Program 会锁住尚未满足前置条件的课节，只有依赖课程被阅读并近期复习后才解锁。这样作者可写出更聚焦、无需重讲前置内容的课程，但也形成过关式学习序列，与间隔重复按个体记忆状态灵活安排复习的方式存在冲突。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/2001372387644563990","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"-gHxi07z\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zSsjk5UvNPGrYp8B6DEFCMS\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Execute Program</a> 的学生无法立刻访问一门课里的所有课节。课程中的大部分课节一开始都是「锁定」的。这些课节依赖该课程中的其他课节：最初会解锁的课节只有{在该课程中没有依赖项的那些}。只有当{其所有依赖项不仅已经被阅读，而且也在近期被复习过（通过内嵌的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z2D1qPwddPktBjpNuwYFVva\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>机制）}之后，课节才会解锁。</p><p data-pid=\"xKo96g6A\">这让课程设计者能够写出更聚焦的课节：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zH26uarYCm9y6tqzuxaGUzt\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Execute Program 的课程假设你对先前材料有扎实的回忆</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>。</p><p data-pid=\"dBz8MVMW\">下面是他们的 UI 对这一机制的解释： </p><figure data-size=\"normal\"><img class=\"origin_image zh-lightbox-thumb\" data-original-token=\"v2-cd09a2c3bf6beabe3c455362d0d8c2ab\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://pic2.zhimg.com/v2-cd09a2c3bf6beabe3c455362d0d8c2ab_r.jpg\" width=\"861\"/></figure><p data-pid=\"AYD85ASM\">这种做法提示了<a class=\"wrap external\" data-draft-title=\"助记媒介可调整为将创制经验逐步展开的形式\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zKRrv2DmKp3VyDEp3oXrKXQ\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">助记媒介可调整为将创制经验逐步展开的形式</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>的一个实例：与其写一本教科书，不如写一串高度聚焦的课节，并在学习者巩固知识的过程中，随着时间推移把它们推送给学习者。但：<a class=\"wrap external\" data-draft-title=\"高效复习安排与过关式课程序列相冲突\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zAFdUuHnU6tNTSTfSK6rJyn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">高效复习安排与过关式课程序列相冲突</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup></p><hr/><p data-pid=\"zB0Glwop\">Q. 为什么 Execute Program 的课节会一直锁定，直到学生完成其前置课程？ <br/>A. 为了让课节可以写得高度聚焦，并且不需要对那些前置课程做任何提醒。</p><h2 id=\"sec-1\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"DV6pBgm6\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-draft-title=\"助记媒介可调整为将创制经验逐步展开的形式\" data-tm-id=\"464367658\" href=\"#/post/464367658\">助记媒介可调整为将创制经验逐步展开的形式</a></li><li data-pid=\"yEnem5q5\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"531644719\" href=\"#/post/531644719\">穿越时间的文本</a></li><li data-pid=\"I5cKWsLx\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"576613520\" href=\"#/post/576613520\">助记文本可以在一段时间内分小段连载，根据读者的记忆情况排期</a></li><li data-pid=\"hODmSXls\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-draft-title=\"高效复习安排与过关式课程序列相冲突\" data-tm-id=\"536966300\" href=\"#/post/536966300\">高效复习安排与过关式课程序列相冲突</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-2\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"a1kSLiu9\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"LmxKl2KQ\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"http://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>感谢主要译者 gpt-5.2-high，校对 Jarrett Ye<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zHLWyC5LVXZLWE9RmoC1gua\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Execute Program’s lessons don’t unlock until you’ve successfully reviewed their prerequisites</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆系统（Spaced repetition memory system） <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"404257681\" href=\"#/post/404257681\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> Execute Program 的课程假设你对先前材料有扎实的回忆 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"2001689461378012509\" href=\"#/post/2001689461378012509\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 助记媒介可调整为将创制经验逐步展开的形式 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"464367658\" href=\"#/post/464367658\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 高效复习安排与过关式课程序列相冲突 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"536966300\" href=\"#/post/536966300\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"2000982862988603503","title":"Execute Program 的课程相当短","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":2,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 助记媒介 & 思想工具"},{"id":"2001689461378012509","title":"Execute Program 的课程假设你对先前材料有扎实的回忆","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":3,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 助记媒介 & 思想工具"},{"id":"464367658","title":"助记媒介可调整为将创制经验逐步展开的形式","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":10,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"576613520","title":"助记文本可以在一段时间内分小段连载，根据读者的记忆情况排期","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":5,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"531644719","title":"穿越时间的文本","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":10,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[],"rec_answers":[]}